I got lucky this game, and managed to kill a long list of monsters
without getting whacked twice myself:-)

Before this character I usually tried to enter minetown with lots of
shoplifted gold and xlev 5, to obtain some protection. Most of the
times, I failed.
I actually got a bit fed up with shoplifting and dying.
This time I figured I'd go to sokoban first, and then the mines. On my
way down me and my pet doggie Jan-Willem passed a scrollshop, And I
couldn't resist. After a bit I got bored tough, not having any tripe:
Jan-Willem wasn't really in the mood for shopping either. As if to
make it up, a fountain djinni offered me a wish one level further
down. I chose GDSM, and resolved not to get my self killed trying for
minetown while I was still on a fairly low level.

I didn't.

I went to sokoban instead to get a BoH, then I went to minetown. There
I found a co-aligned Altar and some water: thus a blessed bag of
holding was now mine. At mines end, I recovered a luckstone.
Jan-Willem got level-teleported though, and when I returned, he didn't
recognise me anymore. I took on a kitten as replacement, having found
some tripe. Somewhere I found a nice polished silver shield and
Demonbane, things were looking good. Also, I had found several /oCM.
#offering them I hoped to get a Vorpal Blade or maybe Mjollnir, but no
such luck:-( I got Cleaver, but I didn't want to give up my reflective
shield.

I found the portal to my quest-level, but I was only level 12, so I
trodded on. Right before medusa I leveled and ate a Wraith-corpse, so
I trodded back. Using telepathy and a ring of levitation I navigated
past the eels and went down to kill some Troll. I was doing better
than my previous characters, who either didn't navigate past the eels
or else got killed by some Troll. The latter left me speed boots, an
oilskin cloak, my dear Vorpal Blade, some cash and of course another
GDSM. Things kept looking good.

after I breezed by medusa and into the castle and the valley of the
dead (gee, a shield of reflection and a ring of levitation. Handy!)
things started to look even better. I found two /oW and got two extra
wishes from the throne in the castle. The only real problem I had was
my teleportitis (why did I ate that nymph again?) but that was quicky
turned into advantage by a brand spanking new ring of teleport
control. I did some scroll and magic marker wishing and I got myself a
helm of telepathy and an "oLS, GoP, a blessed tinning kit and a ring
of slow digestion. I felt ready. I genocided h, ; and L and even E,
though that's really my (newbie) mistake. I thought about an amulet of
reflection but I desided against it. It turns out, I was very happy
with my "oLS.

So I went stalled a sec and wrote some scrolls. AlsoI got some
protection form a priest. Converted his altar, killed the priest,
stole his money, turned his temple into my stash and got some more
protection form another priest. At this point I wanted to burn
Elbereth to complete my stash, but I didn't have a wand of fire. Thanx
to that I did the whole game without Elbereth. I also made some more
holy water and overenchanted my shield of reflection. I liked it
thoug, so I wished for another one: I seemed to have two magic lamps.
By accident I also read one blessed scroll of Enchant Armor while
fully dressed: That explains the +6 GoP. -42AC. (should have been at
least -48 though)

Going further down was a walk in the park. Only Asmodeus' Lair and
Orcus were a bit hard. I did manage to pay off asmodeus for 182
Zorkmids, but his friends had a few cursed scrolls of Create Monster.
Orcus had a wand of death, but that didn't really hurt me. Vlad was
easy, but Rodney keeps hopping around, and that disturbed me. Going
back up was made easy by my controlled teleportitis and the extensive
digging I did. It was made hard by a mysterious force and by rodney
who kept popping up. One time he even popped up with a friend and
killed me. ouch. Who knows what would have happened #twowielding with
an "oR.

At that point I decided to use up my last magic lamp to get 2 blessed
scrolls of charging. For the wand of death:-)

Back on level1 I dropped most of my scrolls and potions, except for
the potion of confusion and a scroll of detect gold. On earth I soon
found the portal, but on the other planes I had to do a lot of
stubling, but somehow I managed to get to the astral plane:-) And
though Death scared me (took 65 of my max HP) I found the altar on my
first try:-)

